From edcdd103d5fb24b7a4a4aa3cd8e815c3d46a5f74 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 02:10:12 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 06/56] fix-sec-3: S-9 residual: the refresh commits FX values
 only in code files, and never test code

- monthly-refresh.yml commit step: after apply, .github/scripts/fx-values-only.mjs (from the tip's
  .github/, which the refresh cannot write) masks the values the FX writer changes in the four code
  copies (FX_PER_USD rows "  CODE: number,", FX_AS_OF, FX_SOURCE, EXTRA_FX_PER_USD, FX_FALLBACK CNY)
  and refuses any other changed line before anything is committed.
- Allow-list: README.md, docs/CONTRACT.md and test/juice.test.js removed. Only detect rules name them;
  no writer writes them (test/juice.test.js holds no pinned FX example: its Big Mac date pin was made
  relational earlier), so the refresh never edits test code.
- test/monthly-refresh-commit.test.js: the allow-list now equals the writers' { file, content } write
  sites; 9de373f's FX hunks (test/fixtures/refresh/fx-refresh-9de373f.json) are committed and deployed;
  six ways of slipping code into an FX copy are refused with nothing pushed.
- docs/DATA_FRESHNESS.md: safety model and pinned values.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_014jaqot5Ddmi7Co6CofBiyc
